    ["……<P_Heart>（刚才我还在房间里，转眼就出现在这个神秘的地方，难不成……是非凡事件！）</>"] = "...<P_Heart> (I was just in my room a moment ago, and in the blink of an eye, I appeared in this mysterious place. Could it be... a Beyonder incident!) </>",
    ["……咳，好重的血腥味。"] = "……Cough, such a heavy smell of blood.",
    ["……茜安，你想不想要一间自己的餐厅，光明正大地做菜？"] = "...Xian, do you want your own restaurant to cook openly?",
    ["　　奥黛丽站了起来，走向门口，对无聊趴坐在外面的金毛大狗笑道：\n　　“苏茜，你这个样子可不够淑女。”\n　　苏茜警惕地左右看了一眼，抽了抽鼻子，然后才开口说道：\n　　“这是猎犬训练时最标准的动作。”\n　　可你并不是合格的猎犬……奥黛丽腹诽了一句，笑着说道：\n　　“我还以为你会这么回答我：奥黛丽，我只是一条狗~”\n　　苏茜认真回应道：\n　　“过于重复的话语容易被别人把握到自身的习惯和心理活动。\n　　“奥黛丽，那本心理学的书上是这么说的。”\n　　……奥黛丽一时竟找不到语言应对。\n\n　　——第四卷《不死者》第十四章 同样的夜晚"] = "Audrey stood up, walked to the door, and smiled at the golden retriever lying bored outside: \n \"Susie, you aren't being very ladylike like that.\" \n Susie looked left and right vigilantly, sniffed, and then spoke: \n \"This is the standard posture for hound training.\" \n But you aren't a qualified hound... Audrey muttered to herself, smiling as she said: \n \"I thought you would answer me like this: Audrey, I am just a dog~\" \n Susie responded seriously: \n \"Excessively repetitive words are easily grasped by others as one's own habits and psychological activities. \n \"Audrey, that's what that psychology book said.\" \n ... Audrey was momentarily unable to find a response. \n \n —— Volume 4 \"Undying\", Chapter 14, The Same Night",
    ["　　感谢您那日陪我完成这趟奇特的旅程。不瞒您说，我至今仍觉得周身萦绕着那罐头的味道，怕是好几天都散不掉。\n　　但您猜怎么着？女儿看了那些照片，笑得前仰后合。她终于愿意跟我聊聊天了——虽然多半是在笑话我，但至少，我们又说上话了。 \n　　她还给我布置了个新任务：把正版《大冒险家》从头到尾读一遍，再写篇读后感交给她。 \n　　另外，那天在码头遇见的后援会朋友邀我们参加下次的活动。女儿听说后，竟说“一起去看看”。我想，这或许是个不错的开始。\n\n又及：那些照片我还留着。每次看到，都觉得……来都来了，总得留点什么。"] = "　　Thank you for accompanying me on this strange journey that day. To be honest, I still feel the smell of that canned food lingering around me, I'm afraid it won't dissipate for several days. \n　　But guess what? My daughter looked at those photos and laughed until she was doubled over. She is finally willing to talk to me—although mostly to make fun of me, but at least, we are talking again. \n　　She also gave me a new task: read the original \"Great Adventurer\" from beginning to end, and write a review for her. \n　　Also, the fan club friend I met at the dock that day invited us to participate in the next event. When my daughter heard about it, she actually said \"let's go see it together\". I think this might be a good start. \n\nP.S.: I still have those photos. Every time I see them, I feel... since I've already come, I have to leave something behind.",
